,"/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years. In 2025 that same pair landed at 49% of normal on the middle, after April to May hit 134% that year. So far in 2026, January to February and February to March each sat at 59% on the middle. Grid 15138 had its driest year in 2005, at 53% of normal.</p>"}
